{"ts": 1784341536.23214, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire 47-frame window. The LONG entry's thesis stayed intact the whole way: price never went net negative after the first minute, climbed from small favorable to a peak near +98pts by t=39m, and settled around +72-92pts for the last third of the window. Against-fires (KMDR/HA/PROPP) appeared repeatedly but never coincided with a sustained breakdown in price -- they were noise inside an otherwise strong uptrend with large absolute giveback tolerance (the leg amplitudes were huge, so even 50-70% giveback still left price deeply favorable). Next time I'd watch for against-fires clustering AT THE SAME TIME price crosses back toward flat/negative, not just when it pulls back from a local high -- that combination never occurred here, which is why bailing was never justified.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 48}
